  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِقْرَاْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَۚ‏(1)\nIQRAA BISME RABBEKAL LAZEE KHALAQ.\nRead in the Name of your Lord who created;\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍۚ‏(2)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN A’LAQ.\ncreated man from a clinging mass.\nاِقْرَاْ وَرَبُّكَ الْاَكْرَمُۙ‏(3)\nIQRAA WA RABBOKAL AKRAMUL.\nRead, and your Lord is the most generous,\nالَّذِىْ عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِۙ‏(4)\nLAZEE A’LLAMA BIL-QALAME.\nwho taught by the pen,\nعَلَّمَ الْاِنْسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْؕ‏(5)\nA’LLAMAL INSAANA MAA LAM YA’LAM.\ntaught man what he did not know.\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَيَطْغٰٓىۙ‏(6)\nKALLAA INNAL INSAANA LA-YATGHAA.\nIndeed man becomes rebellious\nاَنْ رَّاٰهُ اسْتَغْنٰىؕ‏(7)\nAR RA-AAHUS TAGHNAA.\nwhen he considers himself without need.\nاِنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الرُّجْعٰىؕ‏(8)\nINNA ELAA RABBEKAR RUJ-A’A.\nIndeed to your Lord is the return.\nاَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ يَنْهٰىؕ‏(9)\nA-RA-AYTAL LAZEE YANHAA.\nTell me, he who forbids\nعَبْدًا اِذَا صَلّٰىؕ‏(10)\nA’BDAN EZAA SALLAA.\na servant when he prays,\nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَانَ عَلَى الْهُدٰٓىۙ‏(11)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAANA A’LAL HODAA.\ntell me, should he be on [true] guidance,\nاَوْ اَمَرَ بِالتَّقْوٰىۙ‏(12)\nAW AMARA BIT-TAQWAA.\nor bid [others] to Godwariness,\nاَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰىؕ‏(13)\nA-RA-AYTA IN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\ntell me, should he call him a liar and turn away\nاَلَمْ يَعْلَمْ بِاَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَرٰىؕ‏(14)\nALAM YA’LAM BE-ANNAL LAAHA YARAA.\n—does he not know that Allah sees [him]?\nكَلَّا لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَنْتَهِ ۙ لَنَسْفَعًۢا بِالنَّاصِيَةِۙ‏(15)\nKALLAA LA-IL LAM YANTAHE, LA-NASFA-A’M BIN-NAASEYATE.\nNo indeed! If he does not cease, We shall seize him by the forelock,\nنَاصِيَةٍ كَاذِبَةٍ خَاطِئَةٍ ۚ‏(16)\nNAASEYATIN KAAZEBATIN KHAATE-ATAH.\na lying, sinful forelock!\nفَلْيَدْعُ نَادِيَهٗ ۙ‏(17)\nFAL-YAD-O’ NAADEYAHU.\nThen let him call out his gang!\nسَنَدْعُ الزَّبَانِيَةَ ۙ‏(18)\nSA-NAD-U’Z ZABAANEYATAH.\nWe [too] shall call the keepers of hell.\nكَلَّا ؕ لَا تُطِعْهُ وَاسْجُدْ وَاقْتَرِبْ۩‏(19)\nKALLAA, LAA TO-TE’HO WAS-JUD WAQ TARIB.\nNo indeed! Do not obey him, but prostrate and draw near [to Allah]!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Alaq (The Clot)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that whoever recites this Surah in the daytime or at night, and then passes away, he will be counted amongst the martyrs who died while fighting on the side of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is highly recommended to recite this Surah while travelling and it acts as a safety from accidents. If recited on a treasure, it remains safe."
